================================================================================
Code copied from mac4DSTEM
================================================================================

Parts of the app shell, the scripts and the CI workflow are adapted from mac4DSTEM
(https://github.com/mac4DSTEM/mac4DSTEM), Copyright (C) 2026 Paul Lobpreis, GPL-3.0-only; such a file says so in its
first lines. mac4DSTEM's own third-party notices
(py4DSTEM, HyperSpy/eXSpy) apply to the parts it ported and are in its NOTICE.

================================================================================
SpectroKit (a Swift package the app is built with)
================================================================================

The app links SpectroKit (https://github.com/mac4DSTEM/SpectroKit, tag 0.12.0, commit
7e8aa8264adb536d1be230eb81cf11fa02021da0), Copyright (C) 2026 Paul Lobpreis, GPL-3.0-only, for the EDS and EELS rooms: the spectrum image, line
windows and maps, Auto ID, the pooled Cliff-Lorimer quantification, and the EELS alignment, thickness and edge fits. The app embeds its resource bundle
`SpectroKit_SpectroEDX.bundle` in Contents/Resources: the NIST EPQ mass-absorption, line-weight, ionisation cross-section and Krause fluorescence-yield
tables, with the terms and citations in SpectroKit's NOTICE, which applies to them here. For the EELS room it embeds `SpectroKit_SpectroEELS.bundle`: the
generalised oscillator strengths of L. Segger, G. Guzzinati and H. Kohl, "A set of Generalised Oscillator Strengths for the simulation of EELS spectra",
version 1.5.0, Zenodo, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.7645765, licensed under CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/), every K, L and M
table eXSpy uses, values unchanged (SpectroKit's NOTICE). Its eXSpy/HyperSpy and other third-party notices are in its NOTICE.

================================================================================
FormatoKit (a Swift package the app is built with)
================================================================================

The app links FormatoKit (https://github.com/mac4DSTEM/FormatoKit, tag 0.11.0, commit
7e68615ff8812f3d412429c5edc9022fab0639d3), Copyright (C) 2026 Paul Lobpreis, GPL-3.0-only, for its DM3/DM4, Velox EMD, TIFF
and MRC readers and its HDF5 layer, which SpectroKit held until 0.4.0, including the root-attribute file layer
(`HDF5RootAttributes`) the session sidecar is written and read through since FormatoKit 0.5.0: it was this app's own HDF5 binding (an adapted
copy of mac4DSTEM's BraggVectorEMDWriter binding), moved into the kit, and the app no longer carries a copy. Its own third-party notices
(RosettaSciIO, whose rules its adapters port, among them) are in its NOTICE.

================================================================================
DiffractoKit (a Swift package the app is built with)
================================================================================

The app links DiffractoKit (https://github.com/mac4DSTEM/DiffractoKit, tag 0.10.0, commit
317b280dbe35ce1c2e057e2416d3a1be6eaf1d1f), Copyright (C) 2026 Paul Lobpreis, GPL-3.0-only, for crystal structures, the CIF
import, kinematic reflection lists, ring and ellipse calibration and the indexing of a measured |q|. Its scattering table and lattice conventions are py4DSTEM's (GPL-3.0); pymatgen (MIT) was
its oracle and none of its code is copied. Its own third-party notices are in its NOTICE.

