================================================================================
Bundled third-party libraries
================================================================================

The distributed application bundle carries the following libraries as FormatoKit's three dynamic frameworks FormatoLibHDF5, FormatoLibSZ and FormatoLibAEC in
`Contents/Frameworks/` (FormatoKit 0.4.0 and later; embedded and signed by Xcode; macTEM commits none). They are FormatoKit's
vendored binaries with only their install names and the load commands between them rewritten (the code is untouched; FormatoKit's
NOTICE records them); they are redistributed as built there, and their own license terms apply to them rather than the GPL terms above.

HDF5
    https://www.hdfgroup.org/
    Copyright (C) The HDF Group and the Board of Trustees of the University of
    Illinois. Distributed under the HDF5 BSD-style license.
    License text: `Licenses/HDF5-LICENSE.txt`.

libaec (Adaptive Entropy Coding library)
    https://gitlab.dkrz.de/k202009/libaec
    Copyright (C) Deutsches Klimarechenzentrum GmbH. BSD 2-Clause license.
    License text: `Licenses/libaec-LICENSE.txt`.

libsz (szip compatibility interface, provided by libaec)
    Covered by the libaec license above.

The full license text for each ships in the application bundle at `Contents/Resources/Licenses/`, from the `Licenses/`
directory in this repository.

Identity of the three binaries, so that what is redistributed is stated rather than described. SHA-256 of the vendored
files (FormatoKit 0.5.0, tools/xcframework/vendored/) the frameworks are built from; the HDF5 library version string reads
"HDF5 library version: 2.1.1", libaec 1.1.7:

    libhdf5.dylib   d3789c224e6664cd487016a7ef5e71005984f8a04f69a7f643fcdf0332a33491
    libaec.0.dylib  e939c1331d1e8b2dfbfb18c1a5e849e6a60fc7aa748bef4c3ddb5d9ab55451c9
    libsz.2.dylib   2621662e6a3550c5d5f0349146baaa8b85964a25d573a0a2d4b571b14ae8a521

Their provenance and the framework packaging (tools/xcframework/build.sh) are in FormatoKit's NOTICE.

================================================================================
Validation references (used by the test harnesses; not part of the app)
================================================================================

ncempy 1.16 (https://github.com/ercius/openNCEM, tag v1.16, commit f3c09f96dab1d108861db5a6e8477984455c59f3),
GPL-3.0-or-later; its io package is dual-licensed GPLv3/MIT. Installed into the gitignored References/ by
tools/lib/python.sh; tools/parity/metadata-parity compares the metadata macTEM reads against it.

RosettaSciIO (https://github.com/hyperspy/rosettasciio, commit 049e7d7070e84779b499adaf3295beee9facb004),
GPL-3.0-or-later. Its DigitalMicrograph test files are fetched into References/ by tools/lib/fetch-rsciio.sh and read
by tools/parity/metadata-parity; none is committed or distributed.

The committed test fixture macTEMTests/Fixtures/planted-2d.dm4 is synthetic, written by this repository's
tools/parity/metadata-parity/make_dm4_fixture.py.
